==English==
===Etymology===
From {{OE.}} ''[[hæþen]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-iːðən|-iːðən]]

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# not adhering to an [[w:Abrahamic religion|Abrahamic religion]], [[pagan]], adhering to polytheistic beliefs, especially when uncultured or uncivilized. (derogatory)
# by extension, uncultured, uncivilized, savage.
# pertaining to Germanic currents of [[neo-paganism]] known as [[Heathenry]].

====Translations====
{{top}}
*Icelandic: [[heiðinn]]
{{mid}}
{{bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=heathen|pl2=heathens}}

#A person who does not follow an [[w:Abrahamic religion|Abrahamic religion]], a [[pagan]]. (derogatory)
#by extension, an uncultured or uncivilized  person.
# self-designation of some adherents of [[neo-paganism]].

